* LM13700 (one amplifier) simplified model, same pin order as TI's LM13700/NS:
* 1=ABC 2=diode bias 3=+IN 4=-IN 5=OUT 6=V- 7=buffer in 8=buffer out 11=V+
.subckt LM13700_SIM 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 11
* bias input: two junctions above V-
QD1 1 1 m1 QN
QD2 m1 m1 6 QN
QM1 e m1 6 QN
* differential pair
Q4 c4 4 e QN
Q5 c5 3 e QN
* current mirrors to the output
QP1 c4 c4 11 QP
QP2 x4 c4 11 QP
QP3 c5 c5 11 QP
QP4 5 c5 11 QP
QN1 x4 x4 6 QN
QN2 5 x4 6 QN
* Darlington buffer
QB1 11 7 mb QN
QB2 11 mb 8 QN
* diode-bias pin unused in this design
RD 2 6 1G
.model QN NPN(IS=1e-14 BF=200 VAF=100 CJE=1p CJC=1p TF=0.3n)
.model QP PNP(IS=1e-14 BF=80 VAF=60 CJE=1p CJC=1p TF=1n)
.ends LM13700_SIM
